From 31cf9993f67547ec9ffea0468d90333494bee9c2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Jonasz=20=C5=81asut-Balcerzak?= <jonasz@upbound.io>
Date: Mon, 28 Sep 2026 09:38:52 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] feat: align provider runtime with the upjet template
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Replace the Terraform-CLI-era entry point and client with the wiring used by
provider-upjet-civo and upjet-provider-template:

- cmd/provider/main.go: metrics, health probe and webhook servers, poll
  jitter, the secret-cache opt-out, CRD schema stripping in the cache,
  eager conversion webhook registration and gated SafeStart setup. The
  unconditional Setup calls that followed the gated branch are gone; they
  registered every controller twice and left SafeStart inert.
- internal/clients: the setup only carries the plugin-framework provider,
  configured from the credentials secret (API token, or username and
  password); the Terraform CLI flags, the workspace store and the
  redundant framework Configure call are removed. The namespaced
  ProviderConfig now uses a namespace-local secret reference, both
  ProviderConfig kinds expose spec.reconciliationPolicy, and the config
  resolution and credential mapping are covered by unit tests.
- config/templates: the controller template with the reconciliation policy
  reconciler and finalizer, as in civo.
- internal/version replaces config/version.go and keeps the
  crossplane-provider-upcloud User-Agent that UpCloud attributes traffic to.
- cluster/images: distroless static image with the provider binary only;
  the Terraform binary, provider mirror and download variables are gone.
- package/crossplane.yaml: crossplane-contrib metadata and the Crossplane
  version constraint the namespaced resources need.

Generated code is regenerated.

Signed-off-by: Jonasz Małecki <jonasz@upbound.io>
